nt.</div><div data-csa-c-slot-id="customer_review-R1JARTZ5AEZF1P_6_review_text" data-csa-c-type="element" class="a-cardui _Y3Itd_peek-expand_3G9Ub" data-a-card-type="peekExpand" name="a-cardui-deck-autoname-24-card0" data-csa-c-id="etqkeh-4wytgh-pmqq4j-xtrvob"><div class="a-cardui-body _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-reactive-container a-reactive-container-transition"><div><div class="a-cardui-content a-cardui-uninitialized" data-a-max-height="100" style="max-height:100px"><div class="_Y3Itd_relative_1SChh"><div data-hook="reviewRichContentContainer" lang="en-CA" class="_Y3Itd_contain-rich-content_2IORW"><p><span>This little guy is awesome! Our business is just under 1500 square feet of tile floors with a few padded mats, and every morning we come in to the place being spotless.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>Occasionally it gets tangled up in a wire that someone's left around, but other than that it just plain works. I empty the dirty water and refill the clean water every day, because it goes though about 2/3-3/4 of its capacity in a cleaning, but apart from that all I've had to do is wipe down the sensors and self-cleaning tray every week or so.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>Apparently mine has done 95k square feet so far, and it's working just as well as when it was brand new. It's already paid for itself!</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>Totally worth the money (on sale!), highly recommended.</span></p></div></div></div></div><div class="a-reactive-container-gradient"></div></div></div><div data-hook="reviewExpandButtonContainer" class="a-cardui-footer _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer _Y3Itd_read-more-less_2uDYd" data-csa-c-type="widget" data-csa-interaction-events="click" data-csa-c-id="io2zem-fe6ddj-ss1208-3q2l5e"><a href="javascript:void(0)" class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer-button" role="button"><span class="a-expander-icon"><i class="a-css-icon a-css-icon-draw a-css-icon-expand"></i></spa