-list-item"><div data-hook="reviewContainer" data-translatable="false" data-reviewid="R2QF9GIYCB8DM9" data-asin="B0GXF7ZQPY" data-mobile="true" data-locale="en-CA" data-localelanguagename="English" data-sourcelanguage="en-CA" data-sourcelanguagename="English" data-iscustomerrecognized="false" data-iskindleapp="false" data-isandroidapp="false" data-isiosapp="false" data-ismshop="false" data-marketplaceid="A2EUQ1WTGCTBG2"><div id="R2QF9GIYCB8DM9" data-csa-c-slot-id="customer_review-R2QF9GIYCB8DM9_2" data-csa-c-type="widget" data-hook="mobley-review-content" class="a-section a-spacing-large aok-relative" data-csa-c-id="m0rnm7-kuul7g-wp3t5w-gk1c5z"><div data-hook="genome-widget" class="a-row"><a href="/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AE543VUQRH7TWJCA3IX2EBWJ7OQA?ref=cm_cr_dp_mb_bdcrb_top" data-csa-c-slot-id="customer_review-R2QF9GIYCB8DM9_2_profile" data-csa-c-type="element" class="a-profile _Y3Itd_profile-link_2n23E" data-a-size="small" data-csa-c-id="881mgh-29m8qb-8b8cf5-hymxui"><div aria-hidden="true" class="a-profile-avatar-wrapper"><div class="a-profile-avatar"><img src="https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/G/01/x-locale/common/grey-pixel.gif" class="a-lazy-loaded" data-src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX110_.png"></div></div><div class="a-profile-content"><span class="a-profile-name">ItMe!</span></div></a></div><div class="_Y3Itd_single-review-star-rating-bar-mobile_1VEFO"><i data-hook="review-star-rating" class="a-icon a-icon-star-small a-star-small-5 aok-align-center"><span class="a-icon-alt">5 out of 5 stars</span></i><span class="a-letter-space"></span><div data-hook="review-badges"><span data-hook="avp-badge" class="a-size-mini a-color-state a-text-bold">Verified Purchase</span></div></div><h4 class="_Y3Itd_single-review-title_2aKRE" data-hook="reviewTitle" lang="en-CA">The Roborock Qrevo 2 Pro ROCKS! Why did I wait so long to buy this?</h4><div data-hook="review-by-line" class="a-row a-spacing-none"><span data-hook="review-date" class="a-size-small a-color-tertiary">Reviewed in Canada on October 8, 2026</span></div><div data-hook="product-variation-attributes" class="a-row a-spacing-mini"><span data-hook="format-strip-linkless" class="a-size-small a-color-secondary">Colour Name: Black</span></div><div data-hook="reviewTextContainer" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-text-container_325WM"><div data-hook="reviewText" class="a-cardui-deck _Y3Itd_card-deck_37S9P _Y3Itd_mobile_lV1ss" data-a-remove-top-gutter="true" data-a-remove-bottom-gutter="true" name="a-cardui-deck-autoname-18"><div class="a-teaser-describedby-collapsed a-hidden" id="a-cardui-deck-autoname-18-teaser-describedby-collapsed">Brief content visible, double tap to read full content.</div><div class="a-teaser-describedby-expanded a-hidden" id="a-cardui-deck-autoname-18-teaser-describedby-expanded">Full content visible, double tap to read brief content.</div><div data-csa-c-slot-id="customer_review-R2QF9GIYCB8DM9_2_review_text" data-csa-c-type="element" class="a-cardui _Y3Itd_peek-expand_3G9Ub" data-a-card-type="peekExpand" name="a-cardui-deck-autoname-18-card0" data-csa-c-id="e7mxda-pgj4tq-xkj198-yuhp55"><div class="a-cardui-body _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-reactive-container a-reactive-container-transition"><div><div class="a-cardui-content a-cardui-uninitialized" data-a-max-height="100" style="max-height:100px"><div class="_Y3Itd_relative_1SChh"><div data-hook="reviewRichContentContainer" lang="en-CA" class="_Y3Itd_contain-rich-content_2IORW"><p><span>I honestly don’t know why I waited so long to upgrade my robot vacuum. I had an older iRobot for over 10 years, so I knew what a robot vacuum could do, but the Roborock Qrevo 2 Pro is on a completely different level. I’ve only had it a short time, and I’m already a little obsessed with this machine!</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>My house has hardwood floors, tile, area rugs and carpet, so I needed something that could handle different surfaces. I also have a fluffy cat, and between her fur, my own long hair, everyday dust and all the little bits of debris that somehow appear on the floor every day, keeping the floors clean feels like a never-ending job. I wanted something that would actually help take that job off my hands, rather than just give me another gadget to manage.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>So far, this little machine is delivering!  The vacuuming is impressive. It picks up hair, dust and all those little bits of dirt you don’t necessarily realize are there until you see what it collects. There is something ridiculously satisfying about watching it clean and knowing I don’t have to drag out the vacuum myself. I’m especially interested to see how much cat hair it collects over time, because there is certainly no shortage of that in my house!</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>But the mopping is where this machine really won me over.  First of all, can we talk about the little mop pads?! They look like tiny pantaloons, and I absolutely love them. 😂 And when the robot kicks its little “leg” out to mop along an edge, I cannot get over how adorable it is. Who knew a robot vacuum could have so much personality? I find myself watching it work far more than I probably should. It’s ridiculously entertaining for something that is supposed to be doing chores!</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>Beyond being cute, the mopping system is genuinely clever. The robot vacuums and mops, then returns to its dock to wash its own mop pads, refill its water and continue cleaning when needed. When the job is finished, the dock can wash and dry the pads, too. I love that I don’t have to remove the mop pads and wash them myself after every run or constantly stop what I’m doing to tend to the machine.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>The dock is a big part of what makes this system so appealing. It handles so much of the maintenance automatically, which is exactly what I wanted. Yes, the dock takes up some space, but for the convenience it provides, I think it’s well worth it.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>Now, I will say that there is a learning curve. This is not a machine you take out of the box, press one button on, and immediately have everything perfectly set up. It takes time to get to know the machine, learn your way around the app, map out your rooms and customize everything to suit your home.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>Getting the maps right takes some patience, especially if you want to make adjustments, get the rooms organized properly and manually add obstacles or no-go areas so the robot knows where you don’t want it to go. That part can be time-consuming. You need to spend a little time figuring out how you want it to navigate your home and learning where all the settings are in the app.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>At first, there is quite a bit to learn, and you may find yourself going back into the app to change things or fine-tune your maps. But honestly? I think the time spent getting everything set up properly is absolutely worth it. Once you understand how the app works and have your rooms and obstacles mapped the way you want them, you have much more control over how the machine cleans. You can customize the settings to suit your own home instead of having to work around a one-size-fits-all cleaning routine.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>I actually like being able to fine-tune things. I’ve already adjusted the frequency at which it returns to wash its mop pads, setting it to every 20 minutes. I like knowing I can change that depending on how dirty the floors are and what areas I’m cleaning. I’m still learning all the features, but that’s part of the fun of owning it.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>The mapping and app setup are probably the biggest things I would tell a new buyer to be prepared for. Give yourself time, play around with the settings, and don’t expect to have everything figured out on day one. It’s worth putting in the effort rather than rushing through the setup and missing out on the features that make this machine so useful.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>I also love the convenience of having the robot take care of so much on its own. I can let it clean while I get on with my day, and it takes care of washing its mop pads, managing its water and drying the pads when it’s finished. It feels much closer to having a little cleaning helper than simply owning another vacuum.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>I did spend time comparing models before buying because these machines are an investment, and I wanted something that would work for my particular home. Between the mix of flooring, the pet hair and the desire to have both vacuuming and mopping handled with as little manual work as possible, the Qrevo 2 Pro seemed like the right choice. So far, I’m very happy with that decision.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>I’m still in the early days of owning it, so I can’t comment on long-term reliability just yet. But my first impressions are excellent. I love watching it work, I love seeing what it picks up, and I love that I’m spending less time thinking about vacuuming and mopping.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>And yes, I am absolutely entertained by those tiny pantaloons and the little leg that pops out to mop. It’s the little things!</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>My advice to anyone considering this machine: do your research, take the time to set it up properly, learn the app, and be patient while you map your home and adjust the settings. There is a bit of a learning curve, but once you start getting everything dialled in, you can really appreciate what it can do.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>If you have pets, a mixture of flooring, lots of hair and dust, or simply want to spend less time doing floors, I would definitely recommend putting the Roborock Qrevo 2 Pro on your shortlist.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>I went from an old robot vacuum that had served me well for over a decade to this clever little machine, and the difference is remarkable.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>I’m still getting to know all its features, but so far, I’m one very happy owner. The Roborock Qrevo 2 Pro rocks — and those little mop pantaloons have completely stolen my heart! 😂</span></p></div></div></div></div><div class="a-reactive-container-gradient"></div></div></div><div data-hook="reviewExpandButtonContainer" class="a-cardui-footer _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer _Y3Itd_read-more-less_2uDYd" data-csa-c-type="widget" data-csa-interaction-events="click" data-csa-c-id="xehy95-fzfj98-7pbjs7-hozoj0"><a href="javascript:void(0)" class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer-button" role="button"><span class="a-expander-icon"><i class="a-css-icon a-css-icon-draw a-css-icon-expand"></i></span><span class="a-see-more a-color-link"><span class="a-see-more-text" style="">Read more</span><span class="a-see-less-text" style="display:none">Read less</span></span></a></div></div></div></div><div data-hook="translationSpinner" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-translation-spinner-container_ypxf2" style="display: none !important;"><div class="a-spinner-wrapper _Y3Itd_single-review-translation-spinner_1tBUJ"><span class="a-spinner a-spinner-medium"></span></div></div></div><div class="a-row"><div class="a-row a-spacing-small a-spacing-top-small"><span data-hook="helpful-vote-statement" class="a-size-small a-color-tertiary">2 people found this helpful</span></div><div class="a-row a-spacing-top-small"><div class="a-row _Y3Itd_single-review-vote-action-bar_10AyR"><div data-hook="helpfulVoteWidget" class="a-section a-spacing-none _Y3Itd_cr-voting-section_1cNTp"><div class="_Y3Itd_cr-helpful-button_1u3UK cr-vote-component" data-hook="helpfulVoteButton" data-mix-operations="HelpfulVoteClickHandler" data-asin="B0GXF7ZQPY" data-id="R2QF9GIYCB8DM9" data-return-to="